The contract implements a timed asset exchange but fails to validate asset receiver addresses, allowing unauthorized asset transfers.

### Vulnerability: Unchecked Asset Receiver
### Explanation: The contract does not validate the asset receiver address in asset transfer transactions, allowing attackers to redirect assets to arbitrary addresses instead of the intended recipients.
### Risk: High - Assets can be stolen by redirecting transfers to attacker-controlled addresses.
